# why-review.nuon — who read each `why` against its `use`, and what they read.
#
# Spec: `.mi/prd/06-help/01-content-model/prd.md` R5, the clause "`why` only
# where the reason is non-obvious, and never restating what `use` already said".
#
# Why a record and not a check. The restatement is semantic: a competent writer
# restates in different words, so lexical overlap does not see it. Measured
# twice, over the 51 pairs that carry a `why`:
#
#   whole-`why` content-word containment in `use` — corpus mean 0.11, and the
#     known defect `Ctrl+V` scored 0.097, rank 28 of 51, below the mean;
#   best-sentence containment (2026-08-21, finer granularity, to see whether it
#     separated where the whole-text one did not) — corpus mean 0.157, and the
#     known defect `Ctrl+C` scored 0.167 at rank 23 of 51, `Ctrl+Shift+B` 0.143
#     at rank 27. Any threshold that catches them fires on half the manual.
#
# Both proxies are recorded so the next worker does not build a third one. What
# holds the clause instead is a reader — and this file is what stops that being
# a wish. `tests/help-content-model.nu` requires every `why`-carrying entry to
# have a row here whose `digest` matches the exact `use`/`why` pair on disk.
#
# So: **add a `why`, or edit either field, and the gate fails** until someone
# reads the new pair against the restatement rule and records it. That is the
# whole ritual, and it is one line:
#
#   1. read the entry's `use` and `why` together. Does the `why` tell you
#      anything the `use` did not? If not, the fix is to cut it, not to record
#      it. If the `use` is explaining a mechanism, move the mechanism here and
#      leave the gesture there.
#   2. run `nu tests/help-content-model.nu`. It prints the digest to set.
#   3. add or update the row: id, file, digest, reviewer (your session id),
#      date. `note` is optional and carries anything that qualifies the review.
#
# Reviewing your own writing is the one thing this cannot enforce, so it is
# stated instead: rows carrying the "reviewer is also the author" note are
# weaker evidence than the rest, and are the first ones a later reader should
# re-read.
#
# 2026-08-21 · cc-1787301962 swept all 51 pairs. Four were rewritten in that
# pass and carry the note; the other 47 were written by cc-1787250953 /
# cc-1787256992 / cc-1787260422 and read by someone who did not write them.

[
